---
import SaidLayout from "../../../layouts/SaidLayout.astro";
import SaidPlaceholder from "../../../components/SaidPlaceholder.astro";
---

<SaidLayout
  title="Let Claude in — Said guides"
  description="Connect a Claude session to your Said desk over MCP and watch it file its own work under its own name."
  active="guides"
>
  <article class="said-article">
    <h1>Let Claude in</h1>
    <p class="said-meta">One command, a named teammate.</p>

    <p>
      Said speaks MCP — the protocol Claude uses to work with tools. Connected,
      a Claude session can read your boards, search your notes, file cards, move
      them, and leave comments in card threads. Signed, every time, with its own
      name.
    </p>

    <h2>1 · Connect</h2>
    <pre><code>claude mcp add pito-work -- said mcp</code></pre>
    <p>
      That's the whole handshake. The session now carries the desk's tools:
      listing boards, searching, adding and moving cards, commenting, reading
      the exact lines a card references.
    </p>

    <h2>2 · Ask for something real</h2>
    <p>
      Tell Claude to sweep your notes for loose ends and file each one as a card
      with a reference to the lines it came from. Then open the board — the new
      cards are there, each naming the agent that made it.
    </p>
    <SaidPlaceholder
      label="Capture — cards filed by claude, named in history"
    />

    <h2>3 · Work the same card together</h2>
    <p>
      Nobody owns a card. You can be editing while an agent comments; its words
      land in the thread under its name, next to yours. The history keeps
      everyone honest — every move records who, when, and from where.
    </p>
    <SaidPlaceholder label="Capture — a shared thread" />

    <h2>What it can't do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>It can't touch your markdown — your files aren't its to edit.</li>
      <li>It can't act unasked — a session works when you set it working.</li>
      <li>It can't hide — there is no anonymous move in this house.</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</SaidLayout>
